---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
import { pg14Facts } from '../data/facts';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="PostgreSQL 14 End of Life: Upgrade Planning — DatabaseDeveloper"
  description="PostgreSQL 14 community support ends 12 November 2026. RDS and Aurora dates, early minor-version deadlines and a link to the full upgrade checklist."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Time-sensitive guide"
    title="PostgreSQL 14 reaches community end of life on 12 November 2026."
    description="If PG14 is still in production, the immediate job is not panic—it is inventory, target-version choice, compatibility testing, workload baselining and a controlled validation plan."
    primaryLabel="Review upgrade readiness"
    primaryHref="/postgresql-upgrade-readiness"
    secondaryLabel="AWS RDS/Aurora"
    secondaryHref="/aws-rds-aurora-postgresql"
  />
  <section>
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>Current dates</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Milestone</th><th>Date</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>PostgreSQL 14 community fixes end</td><td>{pg14Facts.communityEol}</td></tr>
            <tr><td>RDS and Aurora PostgreSQL 14 standard support ends</td><td>{pg14Facts.rdsStandardSupportEnd}</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Extended Support year-1 pricing begins</td><td>{pg14Facts.rdsExtendedSupportYear1Start}</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Extended Support year-3 pricing begins</td><td>{pg14Facts.rdsExtendedSupportYear3Start}</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Extended Support ends</td><td>{pg14Facts.rdsExtendedSupportEnd}</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="small muted">Dates verified {pg14Facts.verifiedOn}. Re-check provider timelines before scheduling a change.</p>

      <h2>Check your minor version first</h2>
      <p>Some PostgreSQL 14 minor versions reach end of standard support before the major version does. Per the AWS release calendars:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>RDS for PostgreSQL</strong> {pg14Facts.rdsEarlyMinorEnds}</li>
        <li><strong>Aurora PostgreSQL</strong> {pg14Facts.auroraEarlyMinorEnds}</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you are on one of these, you may need a minor-version upgrade before the major-version decision. Either way, test it like a change: baseline first, then compare after. <a href="/insights/postgresql-14-minor-version-deadlines">What RDS does at a minor-version deadline, and how to check your instances.</a></p>

      <h2>What to do first</h2>
      <p>The short version is below. The full <a href="/postgresql-14-upgrade-checklist">PostgreSQL 14 upgrade checklist</a> has the queries, the blockers RDS and <code>pg_upgrade</code> check for, and a PDF copy. If you are on RDS or Aurora, see <a href="/insights/rds-aurora-postgresql-14-extended-support-cost">what Extended Support will cost</a> from 1 March 2027.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Inventory PG14 instances, extensions and client libraries.</li>
        <li>Choose a supported target version based on application constraints and support horizon.</li>
        <li>Capture representative query/workload baselines before the change.</li>
        <li>Test extensions and migrations in a realistic staging environment.</li>
        <li>Compare important plans and latency after upgrade.</li>
        <li>Define rollback criteria before the maintenance window.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Primary sources</h2>
      <p><a href={pg14Facts.postgresqlSource}>PostgreSQL versioning and support policy ↗</a></p>
      <p><a href={pg14Facts.awsSource}>Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL release calendar ↗</a></p>
      <p><a href={pg14Facts.auroraSource}>Aurora PostgreSQL release calendar ↗</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section><div class="container"><CTA eyebrow="Upgrade readiness" title="Still running PostgreSQL 14?" description="Send your platform, current version and extension list. You will get a direct answer on whether a fixed-scope readiness review fits, and what it would cover." primaryLabel="Ask about upgrade readiness" secondaryLabel="See the readiness review" secondaryHref="/postgresql-upgrade-readiness" /></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
